#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179582 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "2574b91a-6534-562b-b4dc-8d95fd19e169" :question/math-academy-id "e-9480" :question/problem "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179583 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "8f09771b-3e0d-567b-a39f-f877bff53372" :question/math-academy-id "e-9481" :question/problem "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "eff8c72f-429d-583a-aa22-f7786f09262a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9484" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\nI. $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\nII. $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\nIII. $1 <     2  <    9$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efe5619c-047f-57cf-a68b-6582ef36b805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177538} {:answer/id #uuid "0809d7b1-2306-5988-a232-bb9ecc7c8380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177539} {:answer/id #uuid "0b3c366a-1c39-520e-8fe5-b79341d95e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177540} {:answer/id #uuid "0f2090ea-3a96-53fa-9848-51207528b6e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177541} {:answer/id #uuid "4a93998e-0289-52f9-9819-d775a1577621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f2090ea-3a96-53fa-9848-51207528b6e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177541} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ecfdc2d-9d95-5ab8-8261-61743a106817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e015992d-dc19-5c46-a968-6f970052cd44" :question/math-academy-id "q-122864" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,4].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}8({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}8({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=8{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=0$ and ${y}_{n}=4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n8{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=8\\cdot 16=128.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a3bc488-a654-58e2-acea-0cde8ca417ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177550} {:answer/id #uuid "add59b06-7aff-5f7b-8180-26392d448211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177551} {:answer/id #uuid "b786bbfd-7079-5e8f-98c4-4aeea35947a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177552} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd66c47-0f50-5072-838a-2f9ab0170ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177554} {:answer/id #uuid "dd41f658-680c-5ade-9061-774bf59f8a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[-2,6]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a3bc488-a654-58e2-acea-0cde8ca417ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177550} :answer-field/id #uuid "aced8254-1be3-536c-8537-7e94eb28d2e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0668e0bd-4637-511c-a263-1fb809d9cda4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122923" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-2,6]?$\n\nI. $\\{-2,-1,0,6\\}$\n\nII. $\\{0,2,4,6\\}$\n\nIII. $-2<2<4<5$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[-2,6].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-2,6]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[-2,6]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0637e47d-67c0-5502-84f3-9b0174a432bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[0,9]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564950} {:answer/id #uuid "81dcfe51-ff64-5d71-bcd4-185222abe7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565140} {:answer/id #uuid "a2db442f-009d-59c4-83fb-5b0ac675dabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565186} {:answer/id #uuid "b03c8658-e3d9-5a74-88b7-3be40d508f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565199} {:answer/id #uuid "fd21c562-ed67-5570-a203-81f2c562ff91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd21c562-ed67-5570-a203-81f2c562ff91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565324} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f92f0b4-0a41-57e7-a39d-64357b2aae64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1be0d7b-0db0-5190-8f45-38feec497f84" :question/math-academy-id "q-122927" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,9]?$\n\nI. $1<5<9$\n\nII. $0<5<7<9<10$\n\nIII. $\\{0,1,2,6,8,9\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,9]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=0.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[0,9]$ since $10$ does not belong to $[0,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[0,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4650d883-0024-5fb8-8a3b-926b85faeb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523398} {:answer/id #uuid "91e31bb5-4dda-578c-be6e-626d6d5b43b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523560} {:answer/id #uuid "962aff86-8fb7-5334-ab89-1ce2ce31f5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[4,8]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523570} {:answer/id #uuid "99d35ace-ff4e-55ea-8ebe-8efeba21fc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523574} {:answer/id #uuid "a79fcbcd-1c42-57fb-8ad9-6ece2081ead7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99d35ace-ff4e-55ea-8ebe-8efeba21fc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523574} :answer-field/id #uuid "97615891-a50f-5ff1-b957-2fefa73efcae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84a42ed7-7cdb-52df-a889-40521b20e8c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122930" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[4,8]?$\n\nI. $4<6<8$\n\nII. $5<6<7<8$\n\nIII. $4<5<6<7$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[4,8].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[4,8]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[4,8]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b01046-18e1-58bb-9aae-addee4a5482b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523302} {:answer/id #uuid "79640bcf-217a-5e27-aca2-3c90383899ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523502} {:answer/id #uuid "84c6b261-478a-5a3c-8af3-eb635d34e070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523534} {:answer/id #uuid "9e84a909-3d25-5602-9873-2133f303f3b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[0,6]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523585} {:answer/id #uuid "cc89bb28-0e81-56bc-b07d-003f53e45ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15b01046-18e1-58bb-9aae-addee4a5482b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523302} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b6f0340-20ad-55e8-b95b-71619bc5062f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e49f5076-911d-5cdf-8140-a000de972953" :question/math-academy-id "q-122934" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,6]?$\n\nI. $0<2<4<8$\n\nII. $\\{0,3,6\\}$\n\nIII. $0<1<3<5<6$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,6]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07280aa0-0a15-5cad-b859-df57e9aa3811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564951} {:answer/id #uuid "28820aa3-a522-5b90-866a-f41417cccf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of $[3,9]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565005} {:answer/id #uuid "5af6f2ec-1bb5-53de-8834-b73287f1f358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565076} {:answer/id #uuid "b86248a1-8983-58de-bd4b-152b44d11496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565216} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ce56cc-ee25-5c68-bd33-78072ae13ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ce56cc-ee25-5c68-bd33-78072ae13ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565303} :answer-field/id #uuid "319bb08e-4683-5c08-aab9-56b1c9e9788e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7147d280-b22a-57e1-b370-a9886ed9abe3" :question/math-academy-id "q-122939" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[3,9]?$\n\nI. $\\{3,5,8,9\\}$\n\nII. $3<4<6<7<8$\n\nIII. $\\{1,3,4,8,9\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[3,9].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[3,9]$  since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[3,9]$ since $1$ does not belong to $[3,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbdbd0b-c1a2-51c0-a8f5-15cb04158568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523478} {:answer/id #uuid "929a1813-87ee-5a94-b302-53b3394322ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523562} {:answer/id #uuid "960de9e7-c3d1-548d-bb28-aea79c7b0d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523569} {:answer/id #uuid "d15c5ee3-1df2-5a89-801e-42aef64a0cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523696} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c61e9b-6f94-5835-aa08-0cb0ef8d2485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbdbd0b-c1a2-51c0-a8f5-15cb04158568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523478} :answer-field/id #uuid "da6d1a46-d11c-5863-8635-3e515e9d04b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28824d9b-0c0b-596c-9f64-75c745081e48" :question/math-academy-id "q-122969" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,8].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,8],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =8-2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56421b11-be0b-5c59-ba07-4a27ea12aeb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565067} {:answer/id #uuid "57339cd1-2256-5617-8f6c-982e93fc9118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565070} {:answer/id #uuid "73462704-1981-5028-8fec-c5d6dc17e1c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565116} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9994d7-bf6e-5198-81f7-14cfcc3177be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565224} {:answer/id #uuid "bedeea4f-2a49-56fe-a4fe-32e000846cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73462704-1981-5028-8fec-c5d6dc17e1c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565116} :answer-field/id #uuid "22ae7436-4bbe-5fcc-854f-c0169c08414a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc3f1bc7-f9c3-504a-985e-91fc4c5b8f28" :question/math-academy-id "q-122970" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-1,5].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}$ is just the length of the interval $[-1,5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+({z}_{3}-{z}_{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}}-{z}_{0})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{z}_{3}}-\\cancel{{z}_{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}+{z}_{q} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}-{z}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07195f6c-4e48-5dcc-aec2-5d69c56026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523272} {:answer/id #uuid "5665712a-009d-5af0-a804-20166b15f257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523431} {:answer/id #uuid "916a6352-92eb-5096-b435-cd193b6feb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523558} {:answer/id #uuid "f878e57d-c65e-5d5e-8918-ff905b1034b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523775} {:answer/id #uuid "ff90e828-6c3f-5567-ad48-f5f15d008572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07195f6c-4e48-5dcc-aec2-5d69c56026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523272} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee43f80-f80a-52f4-830f-025c4b4ca95b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1ddbd77-4be4-59b3-aa0d-217f8714ae20" :question/math-academy-id "q-122971" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-5,5].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[-5,5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-5) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0466c30e-087e-59ca-a910-d62dd06529b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564948} {:answer/id #uuid "0b294371-d2cf-5786-a52b-a3ec80e77916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564956} {:answer/id #uuid "23d6fb4a-c0e9-550f-9034-f8e548969d25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564993} {:answer/id #uuid "ce7b67e1-c08a-5ac9-b206-ac3755f0d0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565247} {:answer/id #uuid "e25bea0f-811e-5d97-897e-71ff469847f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b294371-d2cf-5786-a52b-a3ec80e77916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564956} :answer-field/id #uuid "40d499b8-83d9-584d-a15f-d8ff66161865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8715c2d-ca5b-51c2-9a33-2dfd408c50a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122974" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[5,14].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-2Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $(-2)$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-2Δ{y}_{j}=-2{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[5,14],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =14-5 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-2)\\cdot 9=-18.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e7e2b7-5333-519e-b710-29aad16267c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564941} {:answer/id #uuid "6793c687-c2b2-5217-9580-14080fc036ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565096} {:answer/id #uuid "89411040-8795-5cdc-afcb-a6a871e66201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565152} {:answer/id #uuid "e32e7705-3634-5ead-a672-a3f47e684868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565276} {:answer/id #uuid "e771eb07-8276-52c9-b71a-3b4a1e9b2424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e771eb07-8276-52c9-b71a-3b4a1e9b2424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565283} :answer-field/id #uuid "0711e56e-0fef-5c4e-9ebf-c65efa6dc178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f562602-9739-513b-8ce5-9ee1b6ec86ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-122978" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-8,-1].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}6Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $6$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}6Δ{y}_{j}=6{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[-8,-1],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =(-1)-(-8) \\\\  & =8-1 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n6{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6\\cdot 7=42.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cf29ab3-9af5-5796-9465-f813a4142e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564981} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc3b644-19ca-548e-b453-703cf5bf0c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565031} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb0f8f3-cceb-58b9-8f07-6881841fbb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565105} {:answer/id #uuid "71078581-d224-590e-aece-ba642e26197c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565109} {:answer/id #uuid "c26c4349-ac20-5ab9-8ce1-f10f9aa95ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71078581-d224-590e-aece-ba642e26197c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565109} :answer-field/id #uuid "c921d9f4-e9e5-5990-b776-9a71c2e5fae5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a66dfc35-4f40-599b-91f5-fb79cdcce84b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122987" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[3,8].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=3$ and ${x}_{m}=8$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={8}^{2}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "568b639c-1df2-5465-ae3f-cab03875fcc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565068} {:answer/id #uuid "68f15989-0de0-53f1-af30-851ceb992d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565098} {:answer/id #uuid "6bac9d9b-f57a-5238-be05-6cf4c551208f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565103} {:answer/id #uuid "73360c2e-e156-5ffa-be8e-de6002887e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565115} {:answer/id #uuid "deb437d9-0c5c-5360-9b95-1de1be05df9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deb437d9-0c5c-5360-9b95-1de1be05df9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565270} :answer-field/id #uuid "019097f3-fdab-5454-bc86-1d21ce7596c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dc9a0f07-fee9-5b1d-8ce4-fb565f5e676a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122990" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,5].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=1$ and ${y}_{n}=5$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 24=72.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34bce388-8a83-530c-8716-465e9c3dc065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565016} {:answer/id #uuid "5469ea0b-1a7d-5c68-80b4-70b7cbf036cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565061} {:answer/id #uuid "54d4ac3d-bde5-557b-bc85-c76af89abd05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565062} {:answer/id #uuid "8819dcf4-13cd-534f-9ba0-5764e2cf7081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565149} {:answer/id #uuid "91fb9dca-7989-55a5-9a68-0b46baa2c599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91fb9dca-7989-55a5-9a68-0b46baa2c599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565160} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bc2b85d-9cd8-5e64-a647-58d882625bef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "05eaf340-4492-5bdf-bad0-8c07f4ea4867" :question/math-academy-id "q-122991" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,3].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=1$ and ${x}_{m}=3$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=5\\cdot 8=40.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "154c6ccd-afa9-5d6e-b30d-795512a973b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523300} {:answer/id #uuid "3e17c7a9-6c99-5817-8972-75e58e23f040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "190" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523385} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa8eabe-8df9-5652-9574-6fce6e9ce159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "196" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523387} {:answer/id #uuid "a8cc2c6a-d627-5733-9397-df08623f6047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523611} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c1fe78-e46c-5dc7-811d-7c100ded5e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "198" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8c1fe78-e46c-5dc7-811d-7c100ded5e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "198" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523777} :answer-field/id #uuid "df659612-579e-586d-b30d-ba9a4e631fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "785f4fec-653e-532c-a878-3835d225527c" :question/math-academy-id "q-122994" :question/problem "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,10].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=1$ and ${x}_{m}=10$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={10}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =99.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=2\\cdot 99=198.\n$$"}]}
